  <!-- APPROACH: four habits as rows -->
  <section class="section approach" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head-split">
        <h2 id="approach-title">How I work</h2>
        <p class="lead">Four habits I bring to every engagement.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="habits">
        <li class="habit">
          <h3>Understand the system before changing it</h3>
          <p>Legacy platforms rarely match their documentation. I reverse-engineer how a system actually behaves before changing it, because modernization starts with an accurate picture of what exists.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="habit">
          <h3>Own it past the merge</h3>
          <p>I take features from requirements and design through testing, deployment, and production operation. I design for the operating phase: infrastructure as code, automated and integration tests, and observability with OpenTelemetry and distributed tracing.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="habit">
          <h3>Make the team faster, not just myself</h3>
          <p>I’ve led a development team, reviewed implementation decisions, and mentored engineers. At university I taught and mentored more than 400 students in how real software teams deliver.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="habit">
          <h3>Translate between product and engineering</h3>
          <p>I work closely with Product to turn business requirements into scalable designs and delivery plans that teams can actually execute.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

